astral tactics:  

plane of earth: Kill the wizard, read scroll of cursed gold detection to 
find portal, zap digging wands till you find it.  Put on RoL and RoC, 
ready 4 full healings, make sure armor is right and #twoweapon is set 
corectly.

plane of air: read scroll of cursed gold detect to find portal, hack and 
slash your way there.  If everything is right, this is a yawner.  Air 
Elementals are tough but #twoweaponing with the right weapons (and good 
armor) waxes everything.  If I have to use a full healing, I'm 
dissapointed.  Plus, if you get low on HP, you can hang out in an energy 
vortex to recover.

plane of fire: take off RoC (unless you like to move at a snail's pace), 
read last cursed gold detect scroll.  You get all the fire traps as well 
as the portal, just try them all until you find the portal (you could 
also carry an orb, but they are so heavy). Don't bother fighting, just 
outrun everything.

plane of water: there may be a better way to do this one, but just hang 
out hacking and slashing for about an hour before you run into the 
portal.  If you have auto search/ring of searching it can help.

astral: (make sure you don't have the  RoC on on entry - you need the 
blocking ability of the guardian angel).  always go left or right, that 
way, you shouldn't have to fight two riders at once.  If it turns out 
you've chosen death, turn around and go the other way.  Hack and slash 
through the doorways, run through the rest.  I haven't seen the Tsurugi 
in 3.4 yet, but if you see it, turn and run the other way.  If you get 
to the altar and it's not yours, try the helm of opposite alignment.  If 
that doesn't work then you have to fight your way to another altar.  zap 
famine and pesilence with the WoD.  DO NOT fight death unless you have 
massive range attack (not FoD or WoD - that only makes him stronger).  
You can't tin these guys or write 'Elbereth' around them any more so 
don't waste your time.  You may be able to blind Death, but avoidance is 
the highest percentage.  He's slow and if you've genocided ants and 
snakes, he's not going to catch you.

